      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The answer is straightforward: according to [[credential-scoping]], **the Hub never holds the Anthropic API key in its own process environment at all.** \n\nInstead, a local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it directly into the environment of the spawned child process (either the Ingest or Query agent) immediately before that process starts. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential.\n\nThis design ensures that a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key only exists transiently inside the short-lived child process that actually needs it to call the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5186,
